            {
              "id": "chunk-f5bf85848e61465a3a40ffb5ce3053d8d1d389edd363e44fa5eac7eee5981f18",
              "text": "12.1 Mechanism of Action\nTezepelumab-ekko is a thymic stromal lymphopoietin (TSLP) blocker, human \nmonoclonal antibody IgG2λ that binds to human TSLP with a dissociation constant \nof 15.8 pM and blocks its interaction with the heterodimeric TSLP receptor. TSLP \nis a cytokine mainly derived from epithelial cells and occupies an upstream \nposition in inflammatory cascades.\nAirway and mucosal inflammation are important components of the pathogenesis of \nasthma and CRSwNP. ",
              "metadata": {
                "block_ids": [
                  "doc-tezspire-prescribing-information-section-12-1-p0005"
                ],
                "chunk_config_hash": "a75069450564274f32216a43857bfab5320794c9252075a0132ef0cb43b4cc13",
