            },
            {
              "id": "chunk-c07106f84cc671b601527d1812492c0960a28dfeaaa87517c634ba26a0b20164",
              "text": "Multiple cell types (e.g., mast cells, eosinophils, neutrophils, \nmacrophages, lymphocytes, ILC2 cells) and mediators (e.g., histamine, eicosanoids, \nleukotrienes, cytokines) are involved in airway and mucosal inflammation. \nIncreased levels of TSLP mRNA and protein are found in the airways of patients \nwith asthma as well as in nasal polyp tissue. ",
